TASK 2 — UPGRADE STAGE + RUNG DETECTION
═══════════════════════════════════════════

Update @/lib/mentorContext.ts

Replace current detectTeachingStage with a two-layer detection system:

Layer 1 — TeachingStage (existing): EXPLORE, STRATEGIZE, IMPLEMENT, DEBUG, STUCK, REFLECT
Layer 2 — LearningRung (new, 1-6): maps to the Learning Ladder above

Detection logic for LearningRung:
- Rung 1: history.length < 2, no code, no approach mentioned
- Rung 2: mentions pattern name but with uncertainty words (think, maybe, probably, might)  
- Rung 3: confident pattern name but no code attempted yet
- Rung 4: has code, has errors OR submitCount > 0 with wrong answers
- Rung 5: acceptedCount > 0 but complexity not discussed yet
- Rung 6: acceptedCount > 0 AND complexity discussed in history

Export both stage and rung together as MentorContext type:
  type MentorContext = {
    stage: TeachingStage
    rung: LearningRung  
    tone: ConversationTone
    shouldUpdateSummary: boolean
    allowFullSolution: boolean
  }

Also fix this bug: shouldUpdateSummary currently uses history.length % 3 === 0 
which relies on untrusted client data. Replace with a server-side message counter
stored in MentorConversationSummary.messageCount (add this field to Prisma schema).

